d 'WEBAPI': module to fetch an authenticated JSON web API into Stata as a dataset
d
d  A small, dependency-free generalisation of the "web API from
d Stata" pattern: a request to a URL, an authentication step
d (bearer token, API key, or HTTP basic), and a JSON reply parsed
d back into variables and observations. The HTTP + auth +
d JSON-to-table work is done by a Python standard-library helper,
d so no pip packages or virtualenv are required -- only a working
d python3 on the PATH. webapi get using "<URL>" , records("data")
d [options] webapi post using "<URL>" , body("<json>") [options] 
d
d KW: web api; json; http; rest; oauth; import
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f webapi.ado
f webapi.sthlp
f webapi_helper.py
